    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0500" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50 Recovery/11–1847: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Italy
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-11-18T16:00:00-05:00">November 18,
                            1947—4 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2385. For Allen<anchor n="1" xml:id="d271-f1"/> from Dort<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d271-f2"/>. Although discussions in Congressional committees have
                    not yet been conclusive present trend would indicate Interim Aid will be handled
                    through existing relief machinery and terms of act will require establishment of
                    mission in Paris. Appears quite possible act may be passed within two weeks.
                    Will endeavor commence French shipments at earliest possible moment. Sent Rome
                    as 2385 repeated to Paris as Depts 4258. [Dort.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d271-f1" n="1" xml:id="d271-f1-content">
                <p>Richard F. Allen, Field Administrator, U.S. Foreign Relief Program.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d271-f2" n="2" xml:id="d271-f2-content">
                <p>Dallas W. Dort, Special Assistant to the Assistant Secretary for Economic
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
